{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Oil is extracted from underground reservoirs and refined into fuels, including petrol, diesel and aviation fuel. Liquid fuels are relatively easy to store and transport and have a high energy density. However, oil is finite, burning it releases carbon dioxide, and spills can damage ecosystems. Natural gas is extracted from gas fields and used for heating, industry and electricity generation. It usually releases less carbon dioxide per unit of electricity than coal, but it is still a fossil fuel. Methane leakage during extraction and distribution is an additional environmental concern.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 41.691429, "words": [["Oil", 0.0], ["is", 0.43], ["extracted", 0.65], ["from", 1.242], ["underground", 1.509], ["reservoirs", 2.067], ["and", 2.81], ["refined", 3.053], ["into", 3.704], ["fuels,", 4.052], ["including", 4.783], ["petrol,", 5.41], ["diesel", 5.979], ["and", 6.548], ["aviation", 6.838], ["fuel.", 7.488], ["Liquid", 8.069], ["fuels", 8.545], ["are", 8.963], ["relatively", 9.16], ["easy", 9.799], ["to", 10.124], ["store", 10.286], ["and", 10.693], ["transport", 10.867], ["and", 11.529], ["have", 11.738], ["a", 11.935], ["high", 12.086], ["energy", 12.457], ["density.", 12.91], ["However,", 13.677], ["oil", 14.536], ["is", 14.954], ["finite,", 15.197], ["burning", 16.068], ["it", 16.498], ["releases", 16.684], ["carbon", 17.229], ["dioxide,", 17.612], ["and", 18.46], ["spills", 18.692], ["can", 19.191], ["damage", 19.447], ["ecosystems.", 19.958], ["Natural", 21.444], ["gas", 21.92], ["is", 22.245], ["extracted", 22.396], ["from", 22.965], ["gas", 23.209], ["fields", 23.522], ["and", 23.975], ["used", 24.219], ["for", 24.544], ["heating,", 24.741], ["industry", 25.298], ["and", 25.96], ["electricity", 26.157], ["generation.", 26.819], ["It", 27.945], ["usually", 28.189], ["releases", 28.654], ["less", 29.269], ["carbon", 29.571], ["dioxide", 29.989], ["per", 30.